<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Moulay Ismail</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1645–<a href="/years/1727">1727</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Ismail ibn Sharif</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Moulay Ismail was sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a> from 1672 to 1727, the second ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alaouite-dynasty">Alaouite dynasty</a>. He made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meknes">Meknes</a> a vast imperial city and built the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-guard-morocco">Abid al-Bukhari</a>, an army of enslaved black soldiers. He won back coastal strongholds held by Europeans, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mehdya">La Mamora</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/larache">Larache</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tangier">Tangier</a>, which the English abandoned in 1684.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/moulay-ismail.jpg" alt="Moulay Ismail" width="320" height="515" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Germain Moüette · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ismail_Ibn_Sharif.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
